        "description": "One complete circular outline; no disconnected subfigures, gaps, numerical labels, point labels, arrows or axes. Five radial separators share the same central junction near pixel(203,204). Approximate outer intersections are top(203,17), upper-right(380,143), lower-right(313,345), lower-left(92,349), upper-left(26,151). Pixel positions describe scan structure, not new measured givens. The top-to-upper-right and upper-right-to-lower-right sectors have the same steep diagonal hatching, composing the two-fifths right-hand group. The remaining lower, lower-left and upper-left sectors share the shallower diagonal hatching, composing the three-fifths group. The accompanying complete edition paragraph explicitly identifies the two-fifths cutout and three-fifths remainder as one whole. Exact circular outline and five equal72-degree sectors regularize scan distortion, as required by the edition fractions. Two semantic fill roles replace the two scanned hatch directions. No new displayed numbers, result equation or labels are added. Unlabelled junction coordinates implement the mathematics without adding learner-visible point markers.",
